Hmm wait — for the third test: a ref shipped in files with a space in its name: `files.containsKey(ref)` → continue → then the loop writes files via `AppStorage.appFile(id, file.key)` → file.key = 'i18n/pt-BR (final).json' → invalid → ArgumentError → install fails anyway! So an archive shipping a space-named file still fails at the write loop. Hmm.

Wait — that's the "stricter than before" part: pre-PR the write loop wrote `'apps/$id/${file.key}'` directly — a space-named file wrote fine. Post-PR, `AppStorage.appFile` rejects it → ArgumentError → install fails. The reviewer's suggestion only aligns the i18n-ref VALIDATION message; the hostile-entry write rejection is "by design" per the PR (I3: "hostile-entry-name rejection (an ArgumentError per archive file)"). The reviewer asks the ArgumentError path to have a test — which my first test provides.

So for the i18n alignment: refs not shipped + invalid → honest StateError (not the raw resolver ArgumentError). That's the fix.

But wait — what about `_validateI18nRefs` order vs the write loop: an archive shipping a hostile-named file fails in the loop with ArgumentError — acceptable per PR design (tested now). The i18n-ref fix is only about the *validation* message shape. OK.

Now — should the install fail entirely for a manifest whose i18n ref has an invalid name even when the ref file is ON DISK (update case)? Current: `AppStorage.appFile(id, ref)` throws ArgumentError → install fails with raw message. With fix: `files.containsKey(ref)`? No → `isValidRelativePath(ref)` false → StateError honest message. So an update archive omitting the weird-named ref now fails with the honest message instead of the raw one. Consistent with the "missing" behavior (which also fails the install by design — all-or-nothing). Good.

Now, the copyWith refactor (Thread 3): pure refactor; existing tests cover. I'll rely on the full-suite run.

Also — reviewer Thread 2 mentions `normalizeRefPath` (manifest_i18n.dart:169) accepts spaces while `_segmentPattern` rejects. Let me look at manifest_i18n.dart to understand `refPaths`/refs normalization — the refs in `_validateI18nRefs` come from `LocalizedText.parse(...).refs.values`. Let me check what `refs` holds — normalized or raw paths.

