{"content":"# Thread 3 — 💡 SUGGESTION: third manual 14-field copy — extract a `copyWith`

**Fixed.** `JsAppInfo` now has a single field-preserving `copyWith` (`flutter_app/lib/apps/apps_store.dart`) and both flag setters are one-liners over it:

```dart
JsAppInfo copyWith({
  LocalizedText? nameText,
  LocalizedText? descriptionText,
  String? error,
}) => JsAppInfo(
  id: id, name: name, description: description, icon: icon,
  declaredPermissions: declaredPermissions,
  nameText: nameText ?? this.nameText,
  descriptionText: descriptionText ?? this.descriptionText,
  version: version, chrome: chrome, tileWidget: tileWidget,
  bundled: bundled, platforms: platforms, dirOverride: dirOverride,
  error: error ?? this.error,
);

JsAppInfo withI18nContents(Map<String, String> contents) => copyWith(
  nameText: nameText?.withContents(contents),
  descriptionText: descriptionText?.withContents(contents),
);

JsAppInfo withError(String message) => copyWith(error: error ?? message);
```

`nameText`/`descriptionText` params were needed beyond the suggested `error`-only signature so `withI18nContents` could collapse too — the hand-maintained field list now exists exactly once (plus the primary constructor). First-error-wins semantics of `withError` are preserved. No behavior change; the full `apps_store`/`apps` suite runs green over the refactor.
